NNAAMMEE
     lliinnddeebbuuggffss — Linux file system for debugging

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     lindebugfs              /sys/kernel/debug       lindebugfs      rw 0 0

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The debug file system, or debugfs, makes process debugging easier by pro‐
     viding a simple API for data transfer between the kernel and user space.
     Debugfs is not a general-purpose file system and should not be used as a
     storage medium.  Instead, developers can implement the debugfs interface
     in their code to generate debug information about their program at run‐
     time.  FreeBSD's lliinnddeebbuuggffss uses the pseudofs(9) file system construction
     kit to model itself after Linux's debugfs.  The lliinnddeebbuuggffss API is in‐
     tended for use with programs that take advantage of FreeBSD's LinuxKPI
     compatibility layer.

     When mounted, lliinnddeebbuuggffss will populate with pseudo files from any running
     process that calls ddeebbuuggffss__ccrreeaattee__ffiillee(()).  Since lliinnddeebbuuggffss is a pseudo
     file system, file contents will be generated dynamically based on program
     provided file operations.  The current lliinnddeebbuuggffss implementation formally
     supports seq_file and simple_attr_file virtual file formats.

